From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:25:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: always drop TWT flow state on teardown

mt7915_mac_twt_teardown_flow() returns before unlinking the flow when
the MCU_TWT_AGRT_DELETE command fails, e.g. while the MCU is being
reset. On station removal that leaves a flow embedded in the freed
station on dev->twt_list, which the next TWT setup and the twt_stats
debugfs file then walk.

Release the local state regardless of the firmware result.
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mt7915/mac.c | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mt7915/mac.c b/mt7915/mac.c
index b868cb26..a47ea09f 100644
--- a/mt7915/mac.c
+++ b/mt7915/mac.c
@@ -2411,9 +2411,11 @@ void mt7915_mac_twt_teardown_flow(struct mt7915_dev *dev,
 		return;
 
 	flow = &msta->twt.flow[flowid];
-	if (mt7915_mcu_twt_agrt_update(dev, msta->vif, flow,
-				       MCU_TWT_AGRT_DELETE))
-		return;
+	/* Drop the local state even if the firmware command fails: this is
+	 * also called on station removal and the flow must not stay on
+	 * twt_list after the station is freed.
+	 */
+	mt7915_mcu_twt_agrt_update(dev, msta->vif, flow, MCU_TWT_AGRT_DELETE);
 
 	list_del_init(&flow->list);
 	msta->twt.flowid_mask &= ~BIT(flowid);
